1
00:00:05,095 --> 00:00:08,601
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Makkan Period,

2
00:00:09,017 --> 00:00:10,676
by Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,603
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:13,683 --> 00:00:18,658
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:20,263 --> 00:00:23,983
Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب), he was a hunter.

6
00:00:25,017 --> 00:00:28,267
He would go out and hunt, in the desert

7
00:00:29,244 --> 00:00:35,597
and then he would come back and tell other stories about his hunting expeditions.

8
00:00:36,752 --> 00:00:46,099
So, one day while, he was out hunting, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) approached Rasool Allah ﷺ and started cursing Muhammadﷺ.

9
00:00:46,832 --> 00:00:48,904
While the Messenger of Allah was silent,

10
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:55,251
Rasool Allah ﷺ would not respond to the ignorant words.

11
00:00:56,085 --> 00:00:57,312
وَأَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجَاهِلِينَ

12
00:00:57,352 --> 00:01:01,418
Allah سبحانه وتعالى told Muhammadﷺ, stay away from the ignorant.

13
00:01:02,789 --> 00:01:07,318
The Muslim should not be sidetracked by trivial issues

14
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:11,319
and should not turn the Da'wah(دعوة) into a personal thing.

15
00:01:12,913 --> 00:01:17,206
One should not take it personally, if the insults are directed towards a person,

16
00:01:17,462 --> 00:01:21,510
because that person is calling to Islam, one should not take it personally.

17
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:23,840
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says;

18
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:28,130
فَإِنَّهُمْ لَا يُكَذِّبُونَكَ وَلَٰكِنَّ الظَّالِمِينَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّهِ يَجْحَدُونَ۝

19
00:01:28,473 --> 00:01:29,782
They are not rejecting you,

20
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:35,401
they're rejecting the message that you are presenting them with, that's what they are against.

21
00:01:36,464 --> 00:01:40,738
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ was calm and he did not respond back to Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

22
00:01:41,890 --> 00:01:50,454
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), then threw a stone, a rock at Muhammadﷺ and it hit him in his head and Rasool Allah ﷺ was bleeding.

23
00:01:51,107 --> 00:01:56,813
A slave girl saw that and when Hamza(حمزه) came back from hunting, she went and told him the whole story.

24
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:04,757
Hamza(حمزه) obviously was very upset, when he heard that this happened to his nephew, Muhammadﷺ.

25
00:02:04,941 --> 00:02:08,415
Even though Hamza(حمزه) was a Mushrik(مشرك), a non believer at that time

26
00:02:08,866 --> 00:02:13,098
but because of the relationship between him and Muhammadﷺ

27
00:02:13,509 --> 00:02:18,163
he felt that an attack on Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه was attacked on himself.

28
00:02:18,994 --> 00:02:20,285
So, he walked up to Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

29
00:02:20,325 --> 00:02:24,774
and Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) was sitting with other leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) right in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

30
00:02:25,023 --> 00:02:28,914
And Hamza(حمزه) just came back from hunting and he was still carrying his bow with him.

31
00:02:29,289 --> 00:02:32,801
And he walked up straight to Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) and he hit him on his head with his bow

32
00:02:33,142 --> 00:02:37,077
and said take it and I am now following the religion of Muhammad(محمد).

33
00:02:38,697 --> 00:02:44,996
When Hamza(حمزه) said that, he didn't say it out of conviction, he said it out of pride,

34
00:02:46,193 --> 00:02:48,010
he said it to anger Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

35
00:02:49,273 --> 00:02:54,845
And when that happened and blood was starting to flow out of the head of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل),

36
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:58,197
Bannu Makhzoom(بنو مخزوم), the relatives of Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) stood up to fight Hamza(حمزه),

37
00:02:58,410 --> 00:03:03,128
but then Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) stood up to protect Hamza(حمزه), and they were about to fight,

38
00:03:03,588 --> 00:03:08,423
until Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) interfered and said, No, leave Abu Amarah(ابو عماره) alone, leave Hamza(حمزه) alone,

39
00:03:08,575 --> 00:03:13,478
because I did shamelessly attack his nephew, Muhammadﷺ.

40
00:03:14,795 --> 00:03:16,554
So, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) calm things down.

41
00:03:17,116 --> 00:03:18,431
When Hamza(حمزه) went back home,

42
00:03:18,507 --> 00:03:26,154
there's a narration that states that Hamza(حمزه) went back home and he was surprised that the action he himself took.

43
00:03:27,299 --> 00:03:32,651
And he went back and when his emotions calm down, he started to assess the situation.

44
00:03:32,741 --> 00:03:35,106
I mean, did I do the right thing, what have I done?

45
00:03:35,812 --> 00:03:41,227
And he felt that he was in trouble, because he didn't think it out properly.

46
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:46,666
And he was asking himself, should I become a Muslim or not?

47
00:03:47,839 --> 00:03:54,580
Now, if I want to withdraw, I have already told Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), that I am a Muslim and that's dishonoring.

48
00:03:55,813 --> 00:03:59,205
I mean, in their culture, I mean, it's not right to change your opinion, just like that,

49
00:03:59,263 --> 00:04:03,588
I mean, you say that you're a Muslim, and then the next day, you just change your mind and said, No, I was wrong.

50
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:06,387
So, it was difficult for him to back out.

51
00:04:06,458 --> 00:04:10,780
But then the same thing, it's difficult for him to commit, because he never really thought about it.

52
00:04:11,657 --> 00:04:17,855
So, Hamza(حمزه) said at night, I spent my whole night praying to Allah asking Him to guide me to the truth,

53
00:04:18,328 --> 00:04:21,714
and to tell me, if I have done the right thing or not?

54
00:04:23,155 --> 00:04:30,968
So, he's praying to Allah سبحانه وتعالى at night and saying; O Allah, if this is the right decision, then put the love of it, in my heart.

55
00:04:31,188 --> 00:04:35,261
 If it's the wrong decision, then please O Allah, find the way out for me.

56
00:04:35,826 --> 00:04:39,841
Now, you can notice here that these people used to pray to Allah سبحانه وتعالى

57
00:04:40,143 --> 00:04:42,262
when they would make Dua(دُعَا), they would make Dua(دُعَا) to Allah.

58
00:04:42,766 --> 00:04:45,290
So, their religion was a religion of confusion.

59
00:04:45,843 --> 00:04:51,175
They worshiped Allah, but then they still worshiped other gods, and when we would ask them, why are you worshiping the other gods.

60
00:04:51,369 --> 00:04:55,380
They would say, because these gods are intermediaries between us and Allah.

61
00:04:55,727 --> 00:04:59,261
And then they would say that Allah has daughters, the angels

62
00:04:59,671 --> 00:05:05,648
so it was a big lump of confusion and mixed in, with culture and tradition.

63
00:05:05,986 --> 00:05:12,338
But there was still some traces of the religion of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) in there, for example, they still did Hajj(حَجْ),

64
00:05:12,473 --> 00:05:14,164
even though they did it, in wrong way.

65
00:05:15,081 --> 00:05:17,902
They still gave sanctity to the house of Allahعَزّوجَلّ ,

66
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:24,175
even though they surrounded it with idols but some remnants of the religion of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل) were retained.

67
00:05:26,503 --> 00:05:34,148
Early in the morning Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبد المطلب) said: I woke up and I had my heart filled with love of Islam.

68
00:05:35,039 --> 00:05:39,070
So, I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and I told him that I am a Muslim.

69
00:05:40,128 --> 00:05:47,906
And that was one of the greatest moments for Rasool Allah ﷺ to now have his dear uncle Hamza(حمزه) on his side,

70
00:05:48,612 --> 00:05:50,114
 Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبد المطلب).

71
00:05:52,761 --> 00:05:56,273
So, that's how Hamza رضي الله عنه became Muslim,

72
00:05:56,686 --> 00:06:00,912
obviously, this must have caused agony to Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل).

73
00:06:01,349 --> 00:06:06,891
I mean, Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) would have thought that I have done good by hurting Muhammadﷺ,

74
00:06:06,931 --> 00:06:11,240
but then eventually that was the cause of the Islam of Hamza(حمزه).

75
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:17,430
And that is the Qadar(قدر) of Allah, you never know, what will be the cause of good,

76
00:06:17,969 --> 00:06:19,898
عَسَى أَنْ تَكْرَهُوا شَيْئًا وَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ

77
00:06:19,978 --> 00:06:22,760
You might dislike something, but in it is a lots of good for you.

78
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:26,918
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) thought that he was harming Islam by hurting Rasool Allah ﷺ.

79
00:06:26,958 --> 00:06:32,275
He didn't know that his own action would be the cause of the Islam of Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبد المطلب).

80
00:06:33,350 --> 00:06:34,897
And Ibn Is'haq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says,

81
00:06:34,937 --> 00:06:36,727
 وَكَانَ اِسْلَامُه’حَمِيَّهْ

82
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:43,483
The Islam of Hamza(حمزه) was out of pride, but then it turned into sincerity.

83
00:06:43,871 --> 00:06:46,308
So, initially, it was done with the wrong intention.

84
00:06:46,387 --> 00:06:50,060
He did it just to show Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل) that I'm with my nephew,

85
00:06:51,013 --> 00:06:56,919
but then Allah سبحانه وتعالى changed it, into becoming for the sake of Allah and sake of Allah alone.

86
00:06:56,959 --> 00:07:03,681
And one scholar said that I started studying Islam, to show off and to argue and to debate.

87
00:07:04,346 --> 00:07:09,967
But then after that, the knowledge of the religion of Allah humbled me and I became sincere.

88
00:07:11,344 --> 00:07:17,940
So, I started out with the wrong intention, but then down the line, my intention was being rectified and corrected.

89
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:26,414
So, the religion of Allah, after it stays in the heart for a long time, it draws the person closer and closer to Ikhlaas(إخلاص), sincerity.

90
00:07:27,447 --> 00:07:34,155
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), as we all know, from his early history, was a staunch enemy of Islam,

91
00:07:34,195 --> 00:07:38,686
 and we mentioned how ruthless he was in persecuting the Muslims.

92
00:07:39,611 --> 00:07:45,654
One day, Layla(ليله), the wife of Amir Bin Rabiyah(عامر بن ربيعة), met Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

93
00:07:47,296 --> 00:07:50,221
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told her, Umm Abdallah(ام عبدالله), where are you heading?

94
00:07:51,464 --> 00:07:56,704
She said that you have maltreated us, and oppressed us,

95
00:07:57,301 --> 00:08:02,367
so I'm going to leave to one of God's countries, to worship My Lord.

96
00:08:03,467 --> 00:08:10,065
She was leaving towards Abyssinia and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told her;

97
00:08:10,105 --> 00:08:11,697
صَحِبَتْكِ سَلَامَهْ

98
00:08:12,287 --> 00:08:16,098
May peace be with you, may you Have a safe journey.

99
00:08:16,725 --> 00:08:19,446
That's a very strange statement to come from Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

100
00:08:20,175 --> 00:08:24,098
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) showed no sympathy towards any Muslim, male or female.

101
00:08:25,106 --> 00:08:28,299
So, for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to make Dua(دعا) for this woman

102
00:08:28,339 --> 00:08:33,267
and to say, may peace be with you, may you Have a safe journey, shocked her.

103
00:08:34,237 --> 00:08:37,030
That was the end of the conversation between her and Umar(عُمَر).

104
00:08:37,485 --> 00:08:38,623
And then Umar(عُمَر) left.

105
00:08:39,587 --> 00:08:43,247
When her husband came, she told him, do you know what happened. He said, What?

106
00:08:43,614 --> 00:08:46,707
She said: I met Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), and that was not good news.

107
00:08:47,557 --> 00:08:51,681
And then she said: and he asked me where I was going, and, I told him,

108
00:08:51,955 --> 00:08:57,332
and then he told me in a very sympathetic way, may you have a safe journey.

109
00:08:58,308 --> 00:09:02,866
So, her husband laughed and said, Are you expecting that Umar(عُمَر) will become a Muslim.?

110
00:09:04,150 --> 00:09:06,357
She said: Maybe, why not?

111
00:09:07,325 --> 00:09:08,722
He laughed and said:

112
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:13,859
Umar(عُمَر) will not become a Muslim, until the donkey of his father does.

113
00:09:14,764 --> 00:09:15,717
It's impossible!

114
00:09:16,378 --> 00:09:20,219
HimarAl-Khattab(حِمَارْالخطاب), the donkey of his father will become a Muslim before this man does.

115
00:09:21,139 --> 00:09:23,714
Take that idea out of your mind, forget about it.

116
00:09:24,034 --> 00:09:27,828
This man can't, it's just impossible, he can't become a Muslim.

117
00:09:28,507 --> 00:09:30,493
That was their impression of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

118
00:09:31,925 --> 00:09:34,862
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) narrates and he's narrating his own story.

119
00:09:34,902 --> 00:09:40,444
He's saying that I used to love drinking, I was in love with wine.

120
00:09:41,548 --> 00:09:45,377
And I had some drinking partners whom I would meet every night.

121
00:09:45,890 --> 00:09:49,317
And we used to meet in a place in Hazwara(حزورا).

122
00:09:49,567 --> 00:09:56,107
So, I went late that evening to meet my friends he's going to the pub down the street.

123
00:09:56,718 --> 00:09:59,626
And he didn't find anyone, there was no one there.

124
00:10:00,214 --> 00:10:05,534
He said: So I decided to go to the wine dealer, but I found his shop closed.

125
00:10:06,838 --> 00:10:10,484
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I went around looking for other options.

126
00:10:10,556 --> 00:10:12,802
I didn't find anyone, and it's too late.

127
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:14,984
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said:

128
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:21,819
 Since the pub is closed and the liquor store is closed, then why not go and make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)?

129
00:10:22,518 --> 00:10:23,640
Do something better.

130
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:28,706
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I went to make Tawaf(طواف) around Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

131
00:10:30,499 --> 00:10:32,637
And who do you expect, he found there?

132
00:10:33,229 --> 00:10:37,865
Who else would be praying next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) at that late hour of the night?

133
00:10:39,024 --> 00:10:40,706
Muhammadﷺ.

134
00:10:41,599 --> 00:10:47,050
He said: There was no one there but me and Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه, and Rasool Allah did not sense my presence.

135
00:10:48,267 --> 00:10:55,478
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I wanted to sneak, in one narration to sneak and attack him,

136
00:10:56,161 --> 00:10:58,811
and another narration to listen to what he was reciting.

137
00:10:59,984 --> 00:11:01,044
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

138
00:11:01,084 --> 00:11:07,277
Rasool Allah would pray with Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) in front of him towards the direction of Jerusalem.

139
00:11:08,825 --> 00:11:13,957
Therefore Rasool would be praying towards the wall of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) that had Yemeni(يمني) corner and the Blackstone.

140
00:11:15,118 --> 00:11:16,031
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said:

141
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:21,293
I went from behind and I was hiding between the cloth of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and the Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

142
00:11:21,753 --> 00:11:24,822
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had his back towards the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

143
00:11:25,218 --> 00:11:28,926
and he had the cloth of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) over him, so he cannot see him.

144
00:11:30,029 --> 00:11:34,917
And he said: I was sneaking around the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), until I was right in front of Muhammadﷺ.

145
00:11:35,169 --> 00:11:39,682
Nothing is between me and him except the cloth of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه), but he cannot see me.

146
00:11:41,356 --> 00:11:42,340
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

147
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:48,891
And I was able to hear his recitation, he was right in front of me and he was reciting from Surat-Al-Haaqah(سورةالحاقه).

148
00:11:50,089 --> 00:11:56,223
He said, and I just froze in my tracks, listening to the wonderful words of Qur'an.

149
00:11:57,739 --> 00:12:02,156
And then I told myself, these must be the words of a Poet.

150
00:12:03,552 --> 00:12:07,382
The next Ayah(آية) that Rasool Allah ﷺ recited in Surat-Al-Haaqah(سورةالحاقه) was,

151
00:12:07,407 --> 00:12:10,344
وَمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍ ۚ قَلِيلًا مَا تُؤْمِنُونَ۝

152
00:12:10,638 --> 00:12:13,763
These are not the words of a poet, little do you believe.

153
00:12:14,975 --> 00:12:21,290
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said, I was shocked and I said to myself these must be words of a soothsayer.

154
00:12:21,330 --> 00:12:22,876
 I mean, how did he know what was in my heart?

155
00:12:23,377 --> 00:12:25,354
These must be words, of a soothsayer.

156
00:12:25,537 --> 00:12:26,489
The next Ayah(آية) was

157
00:12:26,524 --> 00:12:29,056
وَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍ ۚ قَلِيلًا مَا تَذَكَّرُونَ۝

158
00:12:29,182 --> 00:12:32,890
These are not the words of a soothsayer, little do you remember.

159
00:12:34,789 --> 00:12:40,487
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: That was the first step in bringing me towards Islam.

160
00:12:41,530 --> 00:12:45,839
I mean, now the foundation of Kuffr(كفر) in the heart of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is cracked.

161
00:12:47,557 --> 00:12:51,929
Nevertheless, His heart is still filled with hatred towards Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims.

162
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:56,334
I mean, he wasn't there yet, He was one step closer, but he's still inhibited

163
00:12:56,389 --> 00:13:00,149
 because of the hatred that he has in his heart towards the Muslims.

164
00:13:01,258 --> 00:13:08,162
One day Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) decided that he's going to bring an end to this misery, to this disunity among Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

165
00:13:08,418 --> 00:13:13,840
 once and for all I'm just gonna go and kill Muhammadﷺ, no matter what happens.

166
00:13:14,817 --> 00:13:17,539
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had this dedication.

167
00:13:17,872 --> 00:13:22,554
He believed that he needs to rid his people from these Sabieen(صابعين),

168
00:13:22,594 --> 00:13:29,004
anyone who would become Muslim they would call them Saba'a(صباء), Sabieen(صابعين), Sabians.

169
00:13:29,564 --> 00:13:31,435
 In other words, they apostated from the religion.

170
00:13:31,719 --> 00:13:33,568
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: I'm going to go and kill him.

171
00:13:33,695 --> 00:13:37,143
He heard that Muhammadﷺ was with 40 of his followers in Dar-Ul-Arqam(دارلأرقم),

172
00:13:37,397 --> 00:13:40,649
he picked up his sword walking down the streets of Makkah alone.

173
00:13:40,881 --> 00:13:47,337
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) knows that he would be killed, if he tries to kill Muhammadﷺ, but he was determined to do it.

174
00:13:48,548 --> 00:13:51,898
Walking down the streets of Makkah who did he meet?

175
00:13:51,978 --> 00:13:56,499
He met one of his relatives who was Muslim in secret, Nu'aim(نُعَيْم).

176
00:13:57,971 --> 00:14:02,019
So, Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) saw Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and he saw evil in his eyes

177
00:14:02,456 --> 00:14:05,289
and anger, he told Umar(عُمَر): Where are you heading?

178
00:14:06,091 --> 00:14:10,004
He said, I'm going towards Muhammad(محمد) to kill him

179
00:14:11,647 --> 00:14:16,115
Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) now has to think on the spot.

180
00:14:17,631 --> 00:14:18,298
What did he say?

181
00:14:18,338 --> 00:14:23,023
Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) said: Why don't you take care of your household first.

182
00:14:24,053 --> 00:14:26,188
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: What's wrong with my household.

183
00:14:26,585 --> 00:14:29,013
Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) said: Your sister has became Muslim,

184
00:14:30,422 --> 00:14:35,760
by saying that Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) has put the sister of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and her husband in danger.

185
00:14:36,639 --> 00:14:37,810
Why didn't Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) do that?

186
00:14:37,995 --> 00:14:41,987
Why would they put Fatima Bint-e-Khattab(فاطمه بنت الخطاب) and her husband in danger.?

187
00:14:42,027 --> 00:14:45,304
He did it because he wanted to save Muhammadﷺ.

188
00:14:46,058 --> 00:14:50,817
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) held Rasool Allah ﷺ in high esteem and they saw that

189
00:14:51,614 --> 00:14:54,373
they could sacrifice their lives if it's going to protect his.

190
00:14:55,243 --> 00:15:01,105
So, Nu'aim(نُعَيْم) told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and this was news to him, that your sister has became Muslim.

191
00:15:02,806 --> 00:15:07,949
And Fatima(فاطمه) was the wife of Saeed Bin Zaid Bin Amr Bin Nufail(سعيد بن زيد بن عمرو بن نفيل),

192
00:15:08,701 --> 00:15:11,904
Saeed(سعيد) is one of the 10 who are given the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

193
00:15:13,210 --> 00:15:18,797
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) changed course and now he was heading towards his sister's house.

194
00:15:20,723 --> 00:15:26,207
Khabbab Bin Arat(خباب بن ارت) was teaching Fatima(فاطمه) and her husband Qur'an.

195
00:15:27,067 --> 00:15:31,252
So, he had a scroll with him and he was reciting to them, Surah-Taha(سورة طه).

196
00:15:32,613 --> 00:15:36,653
When they heard  the footsteps of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), Khabbab(خباب) went into hiding,

197
00:15:36,693 --> 00:15:39,929
and Fatima(فاطمه) took the scroll and she hide it under her thigh.

198
00:15:41,386 --> 00:15:45,979
And then Umar(عُمَر) came in and he said, What was that sound that I heard?

199
00:15:47,340 --> 00:15:48,649
They said, we didn't hear anything.

200
00:15:48,784 --> 00:15:53,596
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Yes, I did hear you recite something, tell me what it was?

201
00:15:54,302 --> 00:15:59,973
And then he said, and I've heard that you are became Muslim and immediately attacked Saeed Bin Zaid(سعيد بن زيد).

202
00:16:00,617 --> 00:16:02,141
And he started punching him.

203
00:16:02,808 --> 00:16:07,620
Fatima(فاطمه) interfered and rose up to defend her husband.

204
00:16:07,755 --> 00:16:10,017
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) hit her in her face.

205
00:16:11,534 --> 00:16:18,640
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw blood flowing out of the face of his sister, he became very sorry.

206
00:16:19,202 --> 00:16:21,043
And he apologized.

207
00:16:22,011 --> 00:16:27,449
She said, I have became Muslim, and my husband is Muslim and do whatever you want.

208
00:16:28,745 --> 00:16:32,763
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: Give me that scroll you were reading.

209
00:16:33,875 --> 00:16:34,763
She said: No.

210
00:16:35,334 --> 00:16:40,563
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) swore in the name of his gods that I'm going to return it back to you.

211
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,373
Give it to me, she said;

212
00:16:42,413 --> 00:16:43,472
 اِنَّكَ مُشْرِكٌ نَجَسْ

213
00:16:43,512 --> 00:16:46,346
You are polytheist, and you are impure.

214
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:50,128
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) went and washed himself and he came back.

215
00:16:50,578 --> 00:16:52,207
So, she gave him the scroll.

216
00:16:52,482 --> 00:16:55,712
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) recited the first verses of Surah-Taha(سورة طه).

217
00:16:56,463 --> 00:16:57,798
طه ۝

218
00:16:58,114 --> 00:17:04,701
مَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ لِتَشْقَىٰ۝

219
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:09,196
إِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِمَنْ يَخْشَىٰ۝

220
00:17:09,512 --> 00:17:16,690
تَنْزِيلًا مِمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْأَرْضَ وَالسَّمَاوَاتِ الْعُلَى۝

221
00:17:17,083 --> 00:17:20,596
 الرَّحْمَٰنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوَىٰ۝

222
00:17:20,904 --> 00:17:28,684
لَهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرَىٰ۝

223
00:17:29,322 --> 00:17:36,044
وَإِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَإِنَّهُ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَأَخْفَى۝

224
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:44,688
اللَّهُ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۖ لَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ۝

225
00:17:45,645 --> 00:17:47,535
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ۝طه۝

226
00:17:48,013 --> 00:17:52,414
We have not sent down to you the Qur'an that you be distressed.

227
00:17:53,430 --> 00:17:56,266
But only as a reminder for those who fear Allah,

228
00:17:56,980 --> 00:18:01,079
 a revelation from He, Who created the earth and the highest heavens,

229
00:18:01,703 --> 00:18:04,786
the Most Merciful, Who is above the throne established.

230
00:18:05,556 --> 00:18:12,973
To Him belongs what is in the heavens, and what is on the earth and what is between them, and what is under the soil.

231
00:18:13,839 --> 00:18:19,499
If you speak aloud, then indeed He knows the secret and what is even more hidden.

232
00:18:19,911 --> 00:18:22,742
 Allah, There is no deity except Him.

233
00:18:23,133 --> 00:18:25,317
To Him belong the best names.

234
00:18:27,027 --> 00:18:32,292
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) went on reciting these words and when he finished he said these are wonderful words.

235
00:18:33,655 --> 00:18:40,771
When Khabbab Bin Arat(خباب بن ارت) heard that he came out of hiding and said: O Umar(عُمَر), I hope that God will choose you,

236
00:18:41,567 --> 00:18:47,511
because I heard the Messenger of Allah yesterday make a Dua(دُعَا) and say, he made a prayer.

237
00:18:48,032 --> 00:18:53,226
Muhammadﷺ made a prayer and said: O Allah guide one of the two Umar(عُمَر)s

238
00:18:53,452 --> 00:18:59,493
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) or Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام) and I hope that you are the one Allah will select.

239
00:19:00,483 --> 00:19:05,027
Rasool Allah ﷺ just one day before, made a prayer.

240
00:19:05,438 --> 00:19:08,018
And said: O Allah, the guide one of the two Umar(عُمَر)s.

241
00:19:08,169 --> 00:19:08,803
and who are they?

242
00:19:08,843 --> 00:19:11,922
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and the other one is Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام), who is Amr Bin Hisham(عمرو بن هشام)?

243
00:19:12,980 --> 00:19:13,776
Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل)

244
00:19:14,912 --> 00:19:20,094
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Allah to strengthen Islam with one of these two men.

245
00:19:21,592 --> 00:19:25,381
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Khabbab Bin Arat(خباب بن ارت), I want to become Muslim.

246
00:19:26,594 --> 00:19:30,733
Where can I meet Muhammadﷺ, Khabbab(خباب) told him go and meet him in Dar-el-Arqam(دار الارقم).

247
00:19:31,854 --> 00:19:36,275
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), went to Dar-el-Arqam(دار الارقم) and he knocked on the door

248
00:19:37,330 --> 00:19:42,545
That was a secret meeting Rasool Allah ﷺ would hold secret meetings with the Sahabah in Dar-el-Arqam(دار الارقم)

249
00:19:42,585 --> 00:19:47,482
because the movement of Islam in Makkah was underground, it wasn't public.

250
00:19:49,777 --> 00:19:54,454
So, one of the companions stood up and he peeked through the door.

251
00:19:55,985 --> 00:19:57,296
And who would you see in front of him.?

252
00:19:57,336 --> 00:19:58,347
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

253
00:19:58,684 --> 00:20:02,722
he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ, it says in the narration that the Sahabi(صحابي) was frightened

254
00:20:03,641 --> 00:20:09,821
and surprised and he told Muhammadﷺ, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is outside and he's carrying his sword too.

255
00:20:11,466 --> 00:20:15,372
Because remember, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) has carried his sword, his intention was to go and kill Muhammadﷺ.

256
00:20:15,412 --> 00:20:17,660
So he was carrying his sword with him.

257
00:20:18,403 --> 00:20:21,735
This companion had all the right to be frightened, I mean, this is Umar(عُمَر).

258
00:20:23,278 --> 00:20:26,897
Now who in that gathering offered to go and open the door.?

259
00:20:27,584 --> 00:20:30,652
Who is the one who can stand up and face Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب),

260
00:20:31,263 --> 00:20:32,309
Who would it be?

261
00:20:32,961 --> 00:20:38,098
Well, Rasool Allah ﷺ did go later on but who was the one who first stood up and said I'm going to go.?

262
00:20:39,436 --> 00:20:40,987
Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب),

263
00:20:41,945 --> 00:20:45,519
the one who would stand up against Umar(عُمَر) was Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب),

264
00:20:45,634 --> 00:20:47,634
he said: O Messenger of Allah,

265
00:20:48,533 --> 00:20:52,522
If Umar(عُمَر) has came for a good reason, we will reciprocate.

266
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:59,628
But if he came with the wrong intentions, then I will kill him with his own sword.

267
00:21:01,865 --> 00:21:05,113
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Hamza(حمزه), no I will open the door for him,

268
00:21:05,286 --> 00:21:09,579
Rasool Allah ﷺ went and he opened the door.

269
00:21:10,100 --> 00:21:13,722
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was one of the tallest men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

270
00:21:14,421 --> 00:21:23,708
when Umar(عُمَر) was Khalifah(خليفه), they received some pieces of cloth, from one of the Islamic States.

271
00:21:25,217 --> 00:21:29,688
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) distributed these clothes evenly, he gave everyone one piece.

272
00:21:31,328 --> 00:21:36,824
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) stood to give Khutba(خطبه), he had two pieces on.

273
00:21:37,665 --> 00:21:38,685
 So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

274
00:21:38,725 --> 00:21:39,685
 اِسْمَعُوْ وَاَطِيْعُوْ

275
00:21:39,725 --> 00:21:40,715
Listen and obey,

276
00:21:41,578 --> 00:21:45,033
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) stood up and said we will not listen and we will not obey

277
00:21:45,893 --> 00:21:47,312
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: How come,

278
00:21:47,661 --> 00:21:53,614
Salman(سلمان) said: Because you have given each one of us one piece and you are wearing two pieces.

279
00:21:55,294 --> 00:22:00,737
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab did not respond, he told his son Abdullah(عبدالله) to stand up and respond to what Salman(سلمان) is saying.

280
00:22:00,864 --> 00:22:03,496
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) stood up and said,

281
00:22:03,835 --> 00:22:09,729
اِنَّ اَبِيْ رَجُلٌ طَوِيْلُ الْقَامَةْ،عَرِيْضُ مُنْكَبَيْنْ فَلَمْ يَكْمِيْ ثَوْبٌ وَاحِدْ، فَعَطَيْتُ ثَوْبِيْ

282
00:22:10,071 --> 00:22:17,786
My father is a very tall man, very well built one piece of cloth would not be nough for him, so I gave him mine.

283
00:22:19,026 --> 00:22:20,131
Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي) said;

284
00:22:20,211 --> 00:22:22,079
 فَلْعَانْ نَسْمَعُوْ وَ نُطِيْعْ

285
00:22:22,119 --> 00:22:24,097
Now we will hear and obey.

286
00:22:24,939 --> 00:22:28,028
So, this was the standard of justice that they had.

287
00:22:29,526 --> 00:22:35,081
Even the Khalifah(خليفه) could not have preference over the masses.

288
00:22:35,984 --> 00:22:42,618
There were people who are willing to stand up and fix the mistakes that they would see.

289
00:22:42,658 --> 00:22:43,647
 اِنْكَارْ اَلْمُنْكَرْ

290
00:22:45,031 --> 00:22:46,346
Like Salman Farsi(سلمان فارسي).

291
00:22:47,261 --> 00:22:50,452
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was not only tall but he was very well built.

292
00:22:51,111 --> 00:22:57,222
And for a while he was a wrestler, he used to wrestle in Makkah at his young age.

293
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:59,567
So, he was a huge well built man.

294
00:23:00,717 --> 00:23:03,532
Rasool Allah ﷺ opened the door for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب)

295
00:23:03,622 --> 00:23:07,508
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was described as being of medium height and medium built.

296
00:23:07,596 --> 00:23:16,463
Rasool Allah ﷺ was not short not too tall, and not very thin but in the same time not a heavyweight, he was medium.

297
00:23:17,078 --> 00:23:19,956
So, you can imagine Rasool Allah ﷺ in front of this huge man,

298
00:23:20,826 --> 00:23:27,155
Rasool Allah ﷺ grabbed Umar(عُمَر) by his clothes and dragged him in and put him down on his knees

299
00:23:28,455 --> 00:23:30,811
and told him: O Umar(عُمَر) when are you going to stop.?

300
00:23:30,851 --> 00:23:33,708
Are you waiting for Allah to strike you with a thunderbolt.

301
00:23:35,418 --> 00:23:39,426
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: O Messenger of Allah I have came to become Muslim.

302
00:23:40,196 --> 00:23:47,067
Now this happened between Rasool Allah ﷺ and Umar(عُمَر), right next to the gate and all of the other Sahabah were in a different room.

303
00:23:47,107 --> 00:23:48,567
So, they didn't see what was happening.

304
00:23:49,250 --> 00:23:52,615
When Umar(عُمَر) said that, Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Allah O Akbar(الله اكبر).

305
00:23:53,448 --> 00:23:57,878
All of the Sahabah knew what has happened, they realized that Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim.

306
00:23:58,138 --> 00:24:00,168
They were so happy with that news.

307
00:24:00,678 --> 00:24:04,481
They made a Takbeer(تكبير) that was so loud, they immediately had to disperse

308
00:24:04,561 --> 00:24:06,630
because it was heard by the people in Makkah.

309
00:24:07,941 --> 00:24:12,130
The Islam of Umar(عُمَر), was a turning point in the history of Islam in Makkah.

310
00:24:12,550 --> 00:24:16,832
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) says, "the Islam of Umar(عُمَر) was victory,

311
00:24:18,284 --> 00:24:25,801
his immigration to Madina was helped to Islam, and his reign, his Khilafah(خلافه) was mercy.

312
00:24:26,807 --> 00:24:28,773
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) says,

313
00:24:29,229 --> 00:24:34,765
We were never able to pray in front of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) publicly, until Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim.

314
00:24:36,229 --> 00:24:41,869
So, an Islam of one person, changed the situation of all of the Muslim community.

315
00:24:42,494 --> 00:24:46,256
That was how valuable Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was, such a great asset.

316
00:24:46,869 --> 00:24:52,412
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) also says that we used to conceal our Islam, until Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim,

317
00:24:52,452 --> 00:24:55,364
then we would proudly proclaim our Islam.

318
00:24:57,635 --> 00:25:03,253
It is mentioned in one of the narrations of Seerah(سيرة) that when Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim,

319
00:25:03,657 --> 00:25:08,444
Rasool Allah ﷺ lined up the Muslims in two ranks.

320
00:25:09,243 --> 00:25:13,524
One rank was headed by Hamza(حمزه), the other rank was headed by Umar(عُمَر).

321
00:25:14,616 --> 00:25:20,639
And they went down the streets of Makkah marching, publicly proclaiming their religion.

322
00:25:20,958 --> 00:25:26,130
While Rasool Allah ﷺ was walking between the two lines, two ranks.

323
00:25:27,919 --> 00:25:34,420
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) became Muslim, he asked and said, Who has the biggest mouth in Makkah,

324
00:25:35,525 --> 00:25:37,603
who's the one who cannot hold water in his mouth,

325
00:25:37,775 --> 00:25:41,326
the one who can publicize this news.

326
00:25:41,366 --> 00:25:43,683
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) didn't want to take it step by step.

327
00:25:43,993 --> 00:25:46,436
He wanted everyone to know that I became Muslim.

328
00:25:47,394 --> 00:25:49,892
They told him Jameel Al-Jumhee(جميل الجماحي),

329
00:25:50,241 --> 00:25:54,733
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said at that time, I was young, but I can still remember everything I see.

330
00:25:55,764 --> 00:26:00,615
He said: I followed my father, and he went to Jameel(جميل).

331
00:26:01,591 --> 00:26:05,385
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Jameel(جميل), he said: Do you know what I did?

332
00:26:05,888 --> 00:26:08,966
Jameel(جميل) said: What.? He said. I've became Muslim.

333
00:26:10,019 --> 00:26:14,759
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said: Immediately as soon as Jameel(جميل) heard the news,

334
00:26:15,013 --> 00:26:19,681
he stood up dragging his gown behind him, his gown was trailing.

335
00:26:19,854 --> 00:26:24,267
And he went running towards the mosque, Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه)

336
00:26:24,556 --> 00:26:28,752
and he went in front of everyone and started screaming to the top of his voice,

337
00:26:29,096 --> 00:26:32,779
O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), Umar(عُمَر) has became Muslim.

338
00:26:33,634 --> 00:26:35,843
He actually said Saba'a(صباعا), he became a Sa'abian.

339
00:26:35,923 --> 00:26:40,970
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is trying to correct the announcement by saying no, I became a Muslim.

340
00:26:41,112 --> 00:26:46,200
But this man is not hearing anything, Umar(عُمَر) is saying he's going around publicizing the news

341
00:26:47,517 --> 00:26:51,484
broadcast it was on national TV, everyone knew that Umar(عُمَر) became Muslim.

342
00:26:52,992 --> 00:26:54,622
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said;

343
00:26:54,931 --> 00:26:57,233
People started flowing towards me.

344
00:26:57,273 --> 00:26:59,097
I mean, Jameel(جميل) did a very good job.

345
00:26:59,819 --> 00:27:01,939
People were just flowing towards Umar(عُمَر).

346
00:27:02,630 --> 00:27:04,014
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said:

347
00:27:04,169 --> 00:27:09,239
So the people surrounded my father from every direction, they were beating him and he was beating them.

348
00:27:10,183 --> 00:27:16,417
They were fighting for hours until the sun was right on top of their heads, and it was too hot for them to continue.

349
00:27:18,050 --> 00:27:20,728
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) went home.

350
00:27:20,989 --> 00:27:24,702
And the people were surrounding his house, they wanted to kill Umar(عُمَر).

351
00:27:24,742 --> 00:27:27,529
I mean, this for them was unbelievable news.

352
00:27:27,569 --> 00:27:29,924
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) becoming Muslim, that's not an easy thing.

353
00:27:30,141 --> 00:27:31,442
So, they wanted to kill him

354
00:27:32,569 --> 00:27:37,155
and Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said: My father was at home and then a man came

355
00:27:37,910 --> 00:27:42,856
and asked my father, he said, What is wrong Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said these people want to kill me.

356
00:27:43,332 --> 00:27:47,416
The man said, No they will not kill you and then he stood outside and said;

357
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:56,547
Leave the man alone, doesn't he have the right to choose the religion he wants to believe in, I am giving him protection.

358
00:27:57,810 --> 00:28:00,154
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said, immediately the people left.

359
00:28:00,753 --> 00:28:05,839
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said, and then later on, I asked my father in Madina and I still had memories of what happened.

360
00:28:05,879 --> 00:28:09,966
 I asked my father in Madina, Who was that man, who came and helped you,

361
00:28:10,432 --> 00:28:13,989
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said, O, my son, that was Al-Aas Bin Wael(العاص بن وائل).

362
00:28:14,401 --> 00:28:16,368
The father of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), he wasn't a Muslim.

363
00:28:17,005 --> 00:28:18,368
That was Al-Aas Bin Wael(العاص بن وائل),

364
00:28:18,821 --> 00:28:21,114
the tribe of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was very small.

365
00:28:22,186 --> 00:28:28,050
And there weren't very strong but their allies were the tribe of Al-Aas Bin Wael(العاص بن وائل).

366
00:28:28,130 --> 00:28:30,876
They were the allies of Bannu Udae(بني عدي) the family of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

367
00:28:30,971 --> 00:28:38,167
So, he came in to help a member of his allies, and he gave Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) protection.

368
00:28:40,092 --> 00:28:43,988
A few notes on this story of the Islam of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

369
00:28:44,337 --> 00:28:48,108
We find here one of the leadership qualities of Muhammadﷺ.

370
00:28:49,157 --> 00:28:55,035
Rasool Allahﷺ knew the personal traits of people, very well.

371
00:28:56,788 --> 00:29:03,196
When Rasool Allah ﷺ made the Dua(دُعَا), the prayer to guide Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) or Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

372
00:29:04,549 --> 00:29:09,254
Why did Rasool Allah ﷺ choose these two people in particular.?

373
00:29:10,612 --> 00:29:22,927
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) had some personal traits that qualified them to be outstanding leaders in whatever area they're in.

374
00:29:24,112 --> 00:29:28,257
These two men were outstanding leaders, both of them.

375
00:29:29,778 --> 00:29:37,655
They had personal qualities that nominated them, to lead people, and to manage their affairs.

376
00:29:39,176 --> 00:29:44,648
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) by the way, is not his name, that's a nickname that was given to him by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

377
00:29:45,753 --> 00:29:49,711
He used to be called by his people before that, Abul Hakam(ابو الحكم),

378
00:29:49,983 --> 00:29:53,911
which is also not his name, but it was a name given to him by his people.

379
00:29:55,042 --> 00:29:56,981
His original name is Amr Bin Hishaam(عمرو بن هشام).

380
00:29:57,974 --> 00:30:01,543
But he was such a wise and intelligent man.

381
00:30:01,852 --> 00:30:05,872
His people called him Abul Hakam(ابو الحكم), which means father of wisdom.

382
00:30:06,706 --> 00:30:14,280
They named him father of wisdom, now when his intelligence did not lead him to Islam.

383
00:30:15,821 --> 00:30:20,448
He became disqualified and he was called Abu Jahal(ابوجَهَل), father of ignorance.

384
00:30:22,024 --> 00:30:24,412
Rasool Allah ﷺ called him father of ignorance,

385
00:30:24,476 --> 00:30:29,564
because no matter how wise a person is, if their wisdom does not lead them to the truth, it's not wisdom.

386
00:30:30,437 --> 00:30:35,198
No matter how intelligent they are, if their intelligence does not lead them to Islam, they have no intelligence.

387
00:30:37,447 --> 00:30:41,237
And that is the admission they will make on the Day of Judgment. Allahسبحانه وتعالى says;

388
00:30:42,182 --> 00:30:47,018
About the people on the day of Judgment, when they realize that they're going to hellfire.

389
00:30:47,563 --> 00:30:52,177
وَقَالُوا لَوْ كُنَّا نَسْمَعُ أَوْ نَعْقِلُ مَا كُنَّا فِي أَصْحَابِ السَّعِيرِ۝

390
00:30:53,046 --> 00:30:58,703
If we had any hearing or understanding or intellect, we wouldn't have been in Hell fire.

391
00:30:59,915 --> 00:31:04,024
Where were our minds, where was our intelligence?

392
00:31:05,558 --> 00:31:12,122
These two men had determination, they have commitment to a cause.

393
00:31:12,939 --> 00:31:20,739
If they believe in something, they are willing to work for it, until the end.

394
00:31:21,970 --> 00:31:26,751
They are relentless in pursuit of their objectives and they are strong.

395
00:31:27,874 --> 00:31:33,502
And in situations of difficulty, they rise above everyone else,

396
00:31:34,251 --> 00:31:37,552
you would find that in every situation that was difficult,

397
00:31:37,759 --> 00:31:44,643
Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) would rise and would lead his people, even though it was an evil, but he did it right.

398
00:31:45,122 --> 00:31:49,248
He was good at what he was doing, even though he was on the wrong path.

399
00:31:49,816 --> 00:31:57,274
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to win one of these men over to Islam, because they would bring with them, all of their resources.

400
00:31:58,323 --> 00:32:01,697
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had these personal qualities.

401
00:32:02,022 --> 00:32:04,792
He had sincerity when he believes in something,

402
00:32:04,967 --> 00:32:10,555
he wouldn't go and in twisted rounds or turns he would face the things straight on, head on.

403
00:32:11,077 --> 00:32:13,660
And he was very courageous and brave,

404
00:32:15,361 --> 00:32:17,656
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was looking at these personal qualities,

405
00:32:17,740 --> 00:32:20,629
See Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) does not have a strong, tribal backing.

406
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:26,130
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab, when he comes to Islam, he will come with his personal qualities not his family background

407
00:32:26,202 --> 00:32:30,989
 because his family background was not that of the noblest in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

408
00:32:31,100 --> 00:32:34,640
 even though he did come from the core tribes of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

409
00:32:34,822 --> 00:32:42,064
But his tribe wasn't a leading tribe, nor were they many numbers to give them such a strong presence in Makkah.

410
00:32:43,080 --> 00:32:47,376
But it was his personal qualities that nominated him to that Dua(دُعَا).

411
00:32:48,261 --> 00:32:55,549
And Allahسبحانه وتعالى destined that he will choose him, out of these two, to become the ally of Islam.

412
00:32:57,240 --> 00:32:59,049
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew the people.

413
00:32:59,780 --> 00:33:05,067
The second lesson to be learned is another leadership quality, that Rasool Allah ﷺ possess,

414
00:33:06,071 --> 00:33:13,274
and that is his deep understanding of the people and how to cure their diseases.

415
00:33:14,315 --> 00:33:21,590
Even though Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) had these excellent personal qualities, but he was suffering from a serious malice.

416
00:33:22,246 --> 00:33:25,893
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), his heart was filled with hatred towards the Muslims.

417
00:33:26,582 --> 00:33:32,642
So, as soon as Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) became a Muslim, Rasool Allah ﷺ knew where the disease was and how to cure it.

418
00:33:33,340 --> 00:33:38,525
It is narrated that Rasool Allah ﷺ placed his hand on the chest of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) and said:

419
00:33:38,565 --> 00:33:44,366
O Allah, cure his heart from hatred and he made that Dua(دُعَا) three times.

420
00:33:45,657 --> 00:33:48,963
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ put his hand on the disease and cured it.

421
00:33:49,950 --> 00:33:53,474
The third quality or the third lesson is,

422
00:33:53,545 --> 00:33:56,974
خِيَارُكُمْ فِيْ الْجَاهِلِيِّهْ خِيِّارُكُمْ فِيْ الْاِسْلَامْ اِذَا فَقِهُوْا

423
00:33:58,006 --> 00:34:05,190
The best of you in Jahiliya(جاهليه), Pre-Islamic era are the best of you in Islam.

424
00:34:06,022 --> 00:34:11,601
Now, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not leave the statement open because this is not the general rule.

425
00:34:13,070 --> 00:34:18,946
It's not necessarily that every person who was good before Islam are going to be good after Islam.

426
00:34:20,700 --> 00:34:24,690
If a person was good before Islam, they have some good personal qualities.

427
00:34:25,195 --> 00:34:31,615
And then they become Muslim, but they deviate within Islam and they don't follow the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

428
00:34:31,685 --> 00:34:35,799
and they don't have good understanding of Islam, they could end up causing more harm than benefit.

429
00:34:36,870 --> 00:34:41,530
And there are many examples of people who had a lot of good personal qualities.

430
00:34:41,761 --> 00:34:46,457
But when they become Muslim, they did not understand their religion correctly,

431
00:34:46,795 --> 00:34:49,854
so they ended up causing a lot of detriment and harm.

432
00:34:50,111 --> 00:34:53,071
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ qualified this statement by saying,

433
00:34:53,111 --> 00:34:54,134
 اِذَا فَقِهُوْ

434
00:34:54,174 --> 00:34:55,888
If they understand.

435
00:34:56,309 --> 00:34:58,122
Fiqh(فقه) means understanding.

436
00:34:58,670 --> 00:35:00,424
Fiqh(فقه) does not mean that you memorize rules.

437
00:35:00,479 --> 00:35:05,386
I mean, now we have used the word Fiqh(فقه) as a label to talk about Islamic law,

438
00:35:05,449 --> 00:35:11,150
but the word Fiqh(فقه) in Hadith(حديث) has a more broader meaning it means understanding, comprehension.

439
00:35:12,052 --> 00:35:19,015
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ says the people who have good personal qualities before they become Muslim,

440
00:35:19,359 --> 00:35:24,899
 they would become the best among the Muslims, if they understand the religion.

441
00:35:25,463 --> 00:35:29,803
 So, there is a prerequisite there, they have to understand the religion.

442
00:35:32,499 --> 00:35:42,837
Ibn Hajar(ابن هجر) states that, when Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) saw that some of the believers had gone to live in a different land and were safe.

443
00:35:43,612 --> 00:35:48,148
The ones, who were in Abyssinia and that Umar(عُمَر) has embraced Islam

444
00:35:49,091 --> 00:35:52,954
They realized that Islam was beginning to rapidly catch on,

445
00:35:53,613 --> 00:36:00,319
they then decided that there would be no solution other than to kill the Prophetﷺ.

446
00:36:01,161 --> 00:36:08,524
Islam has now a branch in Abyssinia and it has a base surviving there.

447
00:36:09,287 --> 00:36:18,051
Inside Makkah, they have won over Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب) and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), things are getting out of control.

448
00:36:18,904 --> 00:36:23,325
Now we have to get beyond our hesitation of killing Muhammadﷺ

449
00:36:23,405 --> 00:36:27,713
because of fear of the retaliation by Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم), we have to do something.

450
00:36:28,625 --> 00:36:37,641
And that led them to the signing of the embargo against Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه

451
00:36:37,681 --> 00:36:43,187
because Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) now officially requested Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) to hand over Muhammadﷺ to kill him.

452
00:36:43,959 --> 00:36:45,769
obviously, Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) refused.

453
00:36:46,562 --> 00:36:52,981
So, the result was an agreement between the various tribes of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to boycott Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

454
00:36:53,582 --> 00:36:58,839
The embargo started in the month of Muharram(محرم) of the seventh year, after the message began.

455
00:36:59,340 --> 00:37:02,216
And it was that no one would deal with them.

456
00:37:02,568 --> 00:37:05,138
No trade would be conducted between them,

457
00:37:05,393 --> 00:37:11,310
and no one would marry of them or to them, until they give up the Prophet Muhammadﷺ.

458
00:37:12,855 --> 00:37:17,045
So, it was a commercial blockade.

459
00:37:17,871 --> 00:37:24,533
And also it was that no family relations are established with them, no marriage, to be done with them.

460
00:37:25,102 --> 00:37:28,972
And they will accept no marriage offers coming from Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

461
00:37:29,770 --> 00:37:34,693
And there are to be surrounded in their enclave, in their neighborhood in Makkah

462
00:37:34,972 --> 00:37:42,291
and the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) wanted to ensure that no food would reach to Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب).

463
00:37:42,811 --> 00:37:47,138
Again, this wasn't only to Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم), but it included Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب),

464
00:37:47,614 --> 00:37:53,344
and Al-Muttalib(ألمطلب) had a very close relationship, with their brethren and from Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم)

465
00:37:53,416 --> 00:37:56,048
and they stood with him in that difficult moment.

466
00:37:56,879 --> 00:38:01,122
And by the way, Al-Imam Al-Shafi(الشافعي) is a descendant of Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب).

467
00:38:01,657 --> 00:38:05,365
So, he is close to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

468
00:38:07,881 --> 00:38:12,084
So, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) came together, and they signed this agreement, the embargo,

469
00:38:12,428 --> 00:38:16,342
and they posted the document, inside Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

470
00:38:17,723 --> 00:38:25,299
Things became quite severe, Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب) were suffering hunger.

471
00:38:26,126 --> 00:38:34,234
And it is reported by Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن أبي وقاص) that we were so hungry that we used to eat leaves of trees,

472
00:38:35,049 --> 00:38:41,047
we would go to the trees and just grab the leaves and eat them, that is how hungry we were.

473
00:38:43,110 --> 00:38:48,074
And these were Mushrikeen(مشركين), by the way, Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب), many of them were non Muslims.

474
00:38:49,052 --> 00:38:50,972
And they went through all of this.

475
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:55,131
 Why? Because they refused to hand over Muhammadﷺ.

476
00:38:56,242 --> 00:39:01,707
So, the embargo includes the Muslims and non Muslims of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم), all of them were included in it.

477
00:39:03,060 --> 00:39:07,919
 Because they refuse to hand over the messenger of Allah, Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

478
00:39:08,891 --> 00:39:10,453
Two or three years past

479
00:39:11,423 --> 00:39:21,028
Al-Hishaam Bin Al-Haris(هشام بن الحارث), who was the most enthusiastic in refusing the terms of the embargo.

480
00:39:21,648 --> 00:39:25,290
He was a relative to Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) from maternal side.

481
00:39:26,464 --> 00:39:31,963
What he used to do during those two or three years is, he would load a camel with food.

482
00:39:32,600 --> 00:39:37,512
And he would take it on top of the hill, that is overlooking the enclave of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

483
00:39:38,284 --> 00:39:43,057
And then he would hit the camel and set it free and release it,

484
00:39:43,441 --> 00:39:48,688
so it would go down the hill and end up among Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم), and he will do that secretly, obviously.

485
00:39:49,222 --> 00:39:55,874
So, he was the one who used to sneak in, food to the people of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب).

486
00:39:56,034 --> 00:39:59,312
Obviously, Hisham Bin Haris(هشام بن الحارث) was not included in the embargo,

487
00:39:59,352 --> 00:40:02,440
because he wasn't himself from Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) or Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب).

488
00:40:02,717 --> 00:40:07,290
But he had some relationship with them through his mother's side.

489
00:40:08,682 --> 00:40:16,172
Hisham Bin Haris(هشام بن الحارث), he went to Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زوهير بن أبي أميه), and he told Zuhair(زهير),

490
00:40:16,902 --> 00:40:29,486
 does it please you that you are eating well and dressing well, while your own uncle's are in that situation of distress.

491
00:40:31,089 --> 00:40:41,139
On my part, I swear that if these people were the uncles of Abu Jahl, Abul Hakam(ابو الحكم) he would not have done so.

492
00:40:41,705 --> 00:40:45,431
 Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زوهير بن أبي أميه) was also a relative of Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم).

493
00:40:46,521 --> 00:40:48,922
They were his relatives from the mother side.

494
00:40:50,039 --> 00:40:59,849
Hisham(هشام) is telling Zuhair(زوهير), how can you accept to see your uncles going through that misery and you do nothing.?

495
00:41:00,890 --> 00:41:03,981
And the one who was calling us to do this is Abul Hakam(ابو الحكم), Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل).

496
00:41:04,500 --> 00:41:08,462
Now, if these were his uncle's, he wouldn't have treated them that way

497
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:11,221
How come we have to go along with this?

498
00:41:11,462 --> 00:41:18,660
You know, it's just like, America is asking from the Muslim countries to boycott such and such a Muslim country.

499
00:41:18,993 --> 00:41:24,726
But then if the same thing was done by Israel, America would never ask for embargo on them.

500
00:41:25,921 --> 00:41:31,825
Imagine if Israel has done similar to what Iraq has done, by the way, they have done more already.

501
00:41:32,606 --> 00:41:39,120
But would America ever asked for, or call for an embargo against Israel(إسرائيل), never.

502
00:41:39,834 --> 00:41:46,451
So, there's a double standard, and Hisham Bin Haris(هشام بن الحارث) was saying Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) is calling us to boycott our uncles.

503
00:41:47,107 --> 00:41:49,039
And he would never do the same to his,

504
00:41:49,547 --> 00:41:55,617
because obviously, Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) was the spearhead of all of these efforts, you would always find the Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) in these places.

505
00:41:57,262 --> 00:42:01,916
Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زوهير بن أبي أميه) responded and said, shame on you Hisham(هشام),

506
00:42:02,908 --> 00:42:05,503
whom am I but one man, what can I do?

507
00:42:06,551 --> 00:42:09,778
In the name of Allah, if I had another person beside me,

508
00:42:11,089 --> 00:42:14,096
I would go about abrogating that document.

509
00:42:14,835 --> 00:42:17,739
Hisham(هشام) said: Well, there's a person with you.

510
00:42:18,826 --> 00:42:22,429
He said, Who was it? myself! I'm going to be with you.

511
00:42:23,229 --> 00:42:26,102
Zuhair(زوهير) said, then find us a third person.

512
00:42:27,131 --> 00:42:31,456
Hisham(هشام) set off to find the third person, he went to Al-Mut'am Ibn Udae(ألمطعم إبن عدئ).

513
00:42:32,513 --> 00:42:38,152
He told Al-Mut'am Ibn Udae(ألمطعم إبن عدئ), Mut'am(مطعم), Are you pleased to have two clans of Bannu Abd Manaf(بنو عبد المناف) suffer,

514
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:41,481
while you look on, in agreement with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) about that,

515
00:42:41,814 --> 00:42:47,363
by God if you enable them to do this, they will soon be treating you the same way.

516
00:42:48,830 --> 00:42:54,758
If we allow this precedence to be set, it could backfire and one day, it could happen to you or me.

517
00:42:56,675 --> 00:43:00,300
Al- Mut'am(المطعم) said: Well, what am I able to do, I'm just one person.?

518
00:43:02,178 --> 00:43:04,809
Hisham(هشام) said: No, you're not one person, there's a second person with you.

519
00:43:04,849 --> 00:43:06,142
Who is it, myself.

520
00:43:07,306 --> 00:43:09,877
Al- Mut'am(المطعم) said: How about you find us a third person?

521
00:43:10,040 --> 00:43:11,411
I did! Who was it?

522
00:43:11,841 --> 00:43:13,062
Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زوهير بن أبي أميه).

523
00:43:13,619 --> 00:43:15,579
Al-Mut'am(ألمطعم) said, find us a fourth.

524
00:43:17,015 --> 00:43:25,442
Hisham(هشام) went to Abul Bukhtari(أبو البختري) and presented to him the same thing and Abul Bukhtari(أبو البختري) said,

525
00:43:25,501 --> 00:43:28,847
Well we need more people, he said, we're now four.

526
00:43:29,331 --> 00:43:31,040
He said go and find us a Fifth.

527
00:43:31,956 --> 00:43:40,328
Hisham(هشام) went, he's doing something, he's working, his lobbying against this oppression of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

528
00:43:41,179 --> 00:43:45,559
So, he went and got a fifth person, which was a Zam'ah Bin Aswad(زمعه بن أسود).

529
00:43:46,705 --> 00:43:52,756
Now they decided that they're going to go and meet at night in Al-Hujoon(إلحجون)

530
00:43:53,156 --> 00:43:55,424
So, they all met together in Al-Hujoon(ألحجون).

531
00:43:55,869 --> 00:44:01,823
And the agreement was that tomorrow morning, we're going to set about destroying this document.

532
00:44:02,159 --> 00:44:05,317
But we're going to make it seem as if it was spontaneous.

533
00:44:06,731 --> 00:44:08,390
So, next day in the morning,

534
00:44:08,787 --> 00:44:17,315
Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زوهير بن أبي أميه) goes in with the special clothes, ceremonial gown that he had on, and he made Tawaf(طواف).

535
00:44:17,879 --> 00:44:21,089
And that was the time in which the assembly of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) meets.

536
00:44:21,244 --> 00:44:25,050
And their meeting place was in An-Nadwa(ألندوى) close by to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

537
00:44:25,500 --> 00:44:29,151
So, Zuhair Ibn Abi Umayyah(زهير بن أبي أميه) is wearing the special clothes, and he made Tawaf(طواف),

538
00:44:29,489 --> 00:44:34,127
and then he came and stood right above the assembly of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

539
00:44:34,923 --> 00:44:42,098
And he told them, O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), does it please you to eat well, and to dress at will,

540
00:44:42,583 --> 00:44:46,395
while Bannu Hashim(بنو هاشم) and Bannu Muttalib(بنو مطلب) are going through distress.

541
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:53,273
I swear In the name of Allah, I'm not going to take a seat unless that document is torn apart.

542
00:44:55,342 --> 00:45:01,726
Now the second person from the five stood up, as if it was spontaneous as if they didn't coordinate this among themselves.

543
00:45:02,188 --> 00:45:06,322
And said, Yes, I never agreed to that document from the day it was written.

544
00:45:07,224 --> 00:45:13,909
And now a third person stood up and said, I swear that I have nothing to do with such a document,

545
00:45:14,074 --> 00:45:16,223
and I don't want to be part of such an agreement.

546
00:45:16,481 --> 00:45:22,011
And the fourth person stood up and then finally Hisham(هشام) himself, gave some comments.

547
00:45:22,846 --> 00:45:28,008
Now Abu Jahal(ابو جَهَل) stood up. And he said:

548
00:45:28,048 --> 00:45:29,859
هَذَا اَمْرٌ دُبِّربليْلْ

549
00:45:29,899 --> 00:45:31,688
This is something that you planned at night.

550
00:45:32,005 --> 00:45:35,155
Don't tell me that it was spontaneous, you planned this aforehand.

551
00:45:36,606 --> 00:45:39,840
But it was too late, things were already getting out of control.

552
00:45:40,223 --> 00:45:44,740
And Al-Mut'am Ibn Udae(ألمطعم إبن عدي), he went into Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) to tear down the document

553
00:45:45,197 --> 00:45:51,925
and Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), he goes in, and he finds that the document has already been eaten up by termites,

554
00:45:52,776 --> 00:45:57,948
with the exception of two words, BismiKallah Hum(بسمك اللهم), in the name of our Lord.

555
00:45:59,930 --> 00:46:05,629
Everything else was eaten, all of the oppression of the document was eaten

556
00:46:05,668 --> 00:46:08,912
 with the exception of the opening words BismiKallah Hum(بسمك اللهم), In the name of Allah.

557
00:46:10,999 --> 00:46:16,943
So, the embargo was ended, after two or three years.

558
00:46:18,118 --> 00:46:26,089
Two lessons to learn from this number one, you see here that five people can make a difference.

559
00:46:27,101 --> 00:46:32,004
The whole embargo was abrogated due to the effort of five people,

560
00:46:32,123 --> 00:46:36,093
actually, it all started by Hisham Bin Haris(هشام بن حارث) alone.

561
00:46:37,263 --> 00:46:43,891
It started as an idea in the mind of this man, and he set about to implement it,

562
00:46:44,331 --> 00:46:46,626
and he recruited a few people around him.

563
00:46:46,847 --> 00:46:52,172
And he brought an end to this corrupt agreement, the agreement of oppression.

564
00:46:53,728 --> 00:47:01,795
So, this shows us the value of organization, five people came together and had an organized plan.

565
00:47:02,002 --> 00:47:05,653
And they were able to bring an end, to the embargo.

566
00:47:06,640 --> 00:47:11,794
So, this is the value of working together, this is the value of having organized work.

567
00:47:12,598 --> 00:47:15,413
And then it shows you that the person needs to take some action.

568
00:47:16,011 --> 00:47:20,679
Hisham(هشام) went to the first person, the first person told him, he gave him a pessimistic view.

569
00:47:21,019 --> 00:47:23,202
He said, I'm only one person, what can I do,

570
00:47:23,984 --> 00:47:25,759
Hisham(هشام) said: We have a second person with you.

571
00:47:25,805 --> 00:47:26,760
 He said, find a third,

572
00:47:26,958 --> 00:47:30,861
Hisham(هشام) set about to find the third, he was a man of action.

573
00:47:31,297 --> 00:47:34,847
And he was able to recruit five people and they made a difference.

574
00:47:35,300 --> 00:47:38,649
Brothers and sisters, this religion needs action.

575
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:43,443
And even though these were Kuffar(كفار) these were Mushrikeen(مشركين) but there's a valuable lesson to learn from this,

576
00:47:43,822 --> 00:47:47,549
that you need to take the first step, you need to do some action.

577
00:47:47,993 --> 00:47:52,496
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ was first given the, Risalah(رسالة),

578
00:47:52,604 --> 00:48:01,164
 see there's one opinion of scholars that Muhammadﷺ became a Prophet, when he received the revelation of Iqrah(إقراء).

579
00:48:01,807 --> 00:48:05,490
 And he became a Rasool where he was given the revelation of

580
00:48:05,545 --> 00:48:06,517
قُمْ فَاَنْذِرْ

581
00:48:07,010 --> 00:48:09,298
That's one view that some scholars hold,

582
00:48:09,734 --> 00:48:12,693
because there's a difference between Nabi(نبي) and Rasool(رسول).

583
00:48:13,011 --> 00:48:19,535
Nabi(نبي), which is translated as Prophet is someone who was receiving revelation from Allah,

584
00:48:19,703 --> 00:48:24,436
but it doesn't necessarily mean that it is a mandate on them to propagate the message.

585
00:48:25,488 --> 00:48:34,367
However, a Rasool(رسول) which is translated as messenger is a Nabi(نبي), who is commanded by Allah to propagate the message.

586
00:48:35,565 --> 00:48:39,857
Rasool Allah ﷺ received the revelation in the verses of Iqra(إقراء).

587
00:48:40,143 --> 00:48:42,076
So, he then became Nabi(نبي).

588
00:48:42,976 --> 00:48:47,212
And then the revelation stopped for a while and he wasn't conveying the message at that time.

589
00:48:47,656 --> 00:48:53,376
He wasn't given the command yet by Allahسبحانه وتعالى to propagate the message, until he was given the revelation of

590
00:48:53,456 --> 00:48:54,193
 قُمْ فَاَنْذِرْ

591
00:48:54,472 --> 00:48:55,531
Stand up and warn.

592
00:48:55,777 --> 00:48:59,788
That is when he became a Rasool(رسول) according to the opinion of some scholars.

593
00:48:59,987 --> 00:49:06,938
So, you can notice that the first commands Allahسبحانه وتعالى gave to Muhammadﷺ, which made him a Rasool,

594
00:49:07,168 --> 00:49:10,535
were the commands of Stand up, stand up.

595
00:49:11,335 --> 00:49:13,724
Rasool Allah ﷺ was wrapped in his garments.

596
00:49:13,977 --> 00:49:17,919
 Allahسبحانه وتعالى said that you have to stand up you can't be sitting down.

597
00:49:18,166 --> 00:49:20,872
You can't be laying on your bed, you have to stand up.

598
00:49:21,246 --> 00:49:25,863
This religion needs men and women to stand up and take action.

599
00:49:26,313 --> 00:49:27,420
قُمْ فَاَنْذِرْ

600
00:49:28,635 --> 00:49:37,103
So, the Muslim is standing up and even when the Muslim is sitting down or laying down, they're not relieved to their duties.

601
00:49:37,994 --> 00:49:40,968
اَلَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ قِيَامًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَىٰ جُنُوبِهِمْ

602
00:49:41,156 --> 00:49:46,430
The ones who remember the name of Allah, standing up sitting down and when they're laying on their beds,

603
00:49:47,075 --> 00:49:48,752
you are never relieved.

604
00:49:49,782 --> 00:49:54,929
 As a Muslim you continuously doing something, so we need to take action.

605
00:49:55,199 --> 00:49:57,589
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) he makes this Dua(دُعَا), he says;

606
00:49:57,629 --> 00:50:00,850
 اَلَهُمَّ اِنِيْ اَعُوْذُبِكَ مِنْ جَلد الْكَافِرْ وَعَجْزِالْمُؤمِنْ

607
00:50:01,054 --> 00:50:06,041
O Allah, I seek refuge in You, from the strong disbeliever and the weak believer.

608
00:50:07,085 --> 00:50:08,535
The believer should be strong.

609
00:50:09,416 --> 00:50:16,478
And unless we stand up and go ahead and do something, things will not change.

610
00:50:17,335 --> 00:50:22,921
We cannot expect our problems to be solved by some supernatural force.

611
00:50:23,776 --> 00:50:32,053
From the time of Musa(موسي) and on, Allahسبحانه وتعالى has not punished a nation through a supernatural event.

612
00:50:32,685 --> 00:50:36,459
For example, with the people of Saleh(صالح) they were destroyed by the Thunderbolt,

613
00:50:36,902 --> 00:50:40,487
with the people of Aad(عاد) they were destroyed through the tornado,

614
00:50:40,741 --> 00:50:44,376
with the people of Loot(لوط) Allahسبحانه وتعالى made the earth sink.

615
00:50:45,336 --> 00:50:54,456
But from Musa(موسى) and onward, Allahسبحانه وتعالى has brought about change through the hands of the believers.

616
00:50:55,042 --> 00:51:01,201
Allahسبحانه تعالى prescribed Jihad(جهاد) on the Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى), they were the first Ummah(امة) to wage Jihad(جهاد).

617
00:51:01,455 --> 00:51:02,763
 It was the Ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى).

618
00:51:03,484 --> 00:51:05,508
Before that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) did not fight.

619
00:51:06,048 --> 00:51:08,127
But from Musa(موسى) and onwards

620
00:51:09,349 --> 00:51:16,920
Allahسبحانه وتعالى would punish the non believers through the armies of al-Mo'mineen(ألمؤمنين), the believers.

621
00:51:17,555 --> 00:51:24,064
 Second lesson, the miracle of the document being eaten up by termites

622
00:51:24,588 --> 00:51:28,545
and this brings up again the issue of the soldiers of Allah.

623
00:51:29,198 --> 00:51:31,406
وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ

624
00:51:31,446 --> 00:51:33,430
No one knows the soldiers of Allah, but He.

625
00:51:34,136 --> 00:51:37,951
I mean, who would imagine that termites would be a soldier for Allah.

626
00:51:38,862 --> 00:51:42,826
So, this is a miracle that happened in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

627
00:51:42,866 --> 00:51:49,256
we can add it to the many other miracles that occurred on the hands of Muhammad صلوات الله وسلام عليه.

628
00:51:51,816 --> 00:51:58,440
Another incident that can classify as a miracle, is the wrestling of Rasool Allah ﷺ with Rukkana(ركانه).

629
00:51:59,116 --> 00:52:02,451
Rukkana(ركانه) was the strongest wrestler in Makkah

630
00:52:02,816 --> 00:52:09,555
Rukkana(ركانه) has never ever lost a wrestling match and he was a non believer.

631
00:52:10,311 --> 00:52:15,214
He came to Muhammadﷺ, and he said: Would you challenge me.

632
00:52:16,547 --> 00:52:20,227
Rasool Allah ﷺ amazingly accepted the challenge.

633
00:52:21,738 --> 00:52:25,220
It seems that Rukkana(ركانه) has done this with the most evil of intentions,

634
00:52:25,290 --> 00:52:28,160
he wanted to humiliate Rasool Allah ﷺ being a Kafir(كافر),

635
00:52:28,200 --> 00:52:33,251
he wants to Ya'ani(يعني) get a chance to lay his hands on Muhammadصلوات الله وسلام عليه,

636
00:52:33,539 --> 00:52:35,666
he didn't know the surprise that was awaiting him.

637
00:52:36,267 --> 00:52:42,598
They started to fight and Rasool Allah ﷺ was able to turn Rukkana(ركانه), upside down and throw him on the ground.

638
00:52:43,660 --> 00:52:45,236
Rukkana(ركانه) couldn't believe what happened.

639
00:52:45,276 --> 00:52:47,613
He stood up again and he tried to fight another time.

640
00:52:47,943 --> 00:52:49,225
Rasool Allah did it, a second time.

641
00:52:50,198 --> 00:52:55,576
And then Rukkana(ركانه) tried a third time and he lost for three times in a row.

642
00:52:56,922 --> 00:53:03,066
Rukkana(ركانه) then said: "Muhammad(محمد), no one has ever put my back on the ground before you

643
00:53:03,837 --> 00:53:07,553
and no one was more hateful in my sight before this, than you.

644
00:53:08,786 --> 00:53:13,494
But now I testify that there is no God but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.

645
00:53:14,865 --> 00:53:18,833
By the way, the deal was that whoever wins gets 100 sheep.

646
00:53:20,068 --> 00:53:22,565
So, this was a bet, this was before betting was made Haram(حرام),

647
00:53:22,589 --> 00:53:25,051
after that betting was made Haram(حرام), but at the time it was allowed.

648
00:53:25,565 --> 00:53:28,089
So, the agreement was whoever wins gets 100 sheep.

649
00:53:28,144 --> 00:53:32,666
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ got the 100 sheep but then he gave him back to Rukkana(ركانه) and said take the sheep.

650
00:53:33,227 --> 00:53:38,274
Rasool Allah ﷺ was able to win three times against Rukkana(ركانه) and that shows us the strength that Rasool Allah ﷺ had.

651
00:53:39,385 --> 00:53:44,822
Rasool Allah ﷺ had the strength of 30 men, this is the second miracle.

652
00:53:44,909 --> 00:53:50,129
Third miracle, the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were continuously asking for a sign, show us a sign

653
00:53:50,319 --> 00:53:57,127
 as if Qur'an was not sufficient, even though Qur'an is the greatest miracle of any Nabi(نبي).

654
00:53:58,207 --> 00:54:03,941
They were asking for a sign, so Allahسبحانه وتعالى revealed to Muhammadﷺ through Jibreel(جبريل),

655
00:54:04,240 --> 00:54:07,857
if they're asking for a sign, we will split for them the Moon.

656
00:54:09,193 --> 00:54:17,693
The moon will be split and the time was set, Rasool Allah ﷺ called the non believers and said, the moon will be split.

657
00:54:18,383 --> 00:54:20,628
And the non believers gathered at night.

658
00:54:21,157 --> 00:54:27,139
And there right in front of them, they saw the moon split into two halves, and then it came back together.

659
00:54:27,787 --> 00:54:38,235
This is a very unique miracle and it is firmly established, in Ahadith(احاديث) in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(المسلم) and in Qur'an.

660
00:54:39,308 --> 00:54:40,824
The Hadith(حديث) and Bukhari(بخاريْ),

661
00:54:41,427 --> 00:54:48,815
Bukhari(بخاريْ) mentions that the splitting of the moon came between the embracing of Islam of Umar(عُمَر) and after the migration to Abyssinia.

662
00:54:49,363 --> 00:54:55,552
And in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم), it states that the Makkan people requested Allah's Apostle to show them a miracle,

663
00:54:56,058 --> 00:54:58,532
and so he showed them the splitting of the moon.

664
00:54:59,175 --> 00:55:01,078
Again in Muslim(مسلم) another Hadith(حديث).

665
00:55:01,412 --> 00:55:05,238
This Hadith(حديث) has been transmitted on the authority of Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود), who said;

666
00:55:05,663 --> 00:55:09,218
We were along with the Allah's Messenger May peace be upon him at Mina(مناء).

667
00:55:09,612 --> 00:55:17,818
The moon was split up into two, one of its parts was behind the mountain, and the other one was on this side of the mountain.

668
00:55:18,213 --> 00:55:23,191
Allah's Messenger May peace be upon him said to us; bear witness to this.

669
00:55:23,880 --> 00:55:25,600
Allah سبحانه وتعالى says,

670
00:55:26,532 --> 00:55:31,592
اِقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ وَانْشَقَّ الْقَمَرُ ۝

671
00:55:32,656 --> 00:55:39,863
وَإِنْ يَرَوْا آيَةً يُعْرِضُوا وَيَقُولُوا سِحْرٌ مُسْتَمِرٌّ۝

672
00:55:40,162 --> 00:55:42,282
When they saw the sign of Allah, what did they say?

673
00:55:43,196 --> 00:55:46,987
They said: He threw or cast magic on our eyes.

674
00:55:48,206 --> 00:55:53,708
Allahسبحانه وتعالى says the hour of Judgment is near and the moon is cleft asunder.

675
00:55:54,112 --> 00:55:58,771
But if they see a sign, they turn away and say this is but transient magic.

676
00:55:59,810 --> 00:56:03,468
They accused Muhammadﷺ of performing magic,

677
00:56:04,707 --> 00:56:10,236
